2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Kierstede was born circa 1612.
2 CONT John Reynolds Totten, "Anneke Jans (1607-8?-1663) and Her Two Husbands", New York Genealogical & Biographical Record Vol. 56, pages 202-243 (1925): p.208.
2 CONT William B. Bogardus,"Anneke Jans and Everardus Bogardus Descendants Website", online www.freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/*ghosthunter/Anneke/page0.htm.. , Chart No.1. Born abt 1612/1616.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Sara Roelofse, daughter of Roeloff Jansen and Anneke Jans, at Reformed Dutch Church, New Amsterdam, on 29 June 1642; "Mr. Hans Kierstede, Chirurgyn, j.m. Van Maegdenburg, en Sara Roelofs, j.d. Van Amsterdam, beyde wonen
2 CONC de tot N. Amsterdam."
2 CONT Samuel S. Purple, Records of the Reformed Dutch Church in New Amsterdam and New York; Marriages from 11 December 1639 to 26 August 1801 (Bowie, MD: Heritage Books, reprint 2003, original 1890 NYG&BS), p.11.
2 CONT
2 CONT A surgeon. From Maegdenburg, Prussian Saxony, perhaps a refugee of that place after it was sacked by Tilly in 1630. He came to New Netherlands in 1638, with Director General Kieft in the service of the West India Co. He was the fi
2 CONC rst physician and surgeon in New Amsterdam. His brother Jochem Kierstede perished in the wreck of "The Princess" off the coast of Wales, along with Kieft and Dom. Bogardus. He appears in the early Dutch records on 1 May 1638; on 2
2 CONC 8 Aug1648 he is spoken of as "late in the service of the W.I. Co." He was alive when his last child was baptized on 13 Sep 1665 and on 17 Jul 1667 he is spoken of on a deed as "being then dead."
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Frans Harmensen Van de Bogart , son of Harmen Myndertszen Van de Bogart and Gillisje Claese Schouw, on 26 August 1640 at Reformed Dutch Church, New Amsterdam, (sponsors Marin Ederlaen, Corn. Leenderts, Mr.
2 CONC  Hans Kierstede, Aeriaentje Cornelis).
2 CONT "Records of the Reformed Dutch Church in New York", New York Genealogical and Biographical Record Vols.5- (1874-): 5:28. Francoys; parents: Mr. Herman Meynderts; witnesses: Marin Ederiaen, Corn. Leenderts, Mr. Hans Kierstede, Aeri
2 CONC aentje Cornelis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Isaac Verplanck , son of Abraham Isaacsen Verplanck and Maria Vigne, on 16 June 1641 at Reformed Dutch Church, New Amsterdam, (sponsors Mr. Hans Kierstede, Secy; Corn. Van Tienhoven, Maurice Janszen, Rache
2 CONC l Vynen).
2 CONT Ibid., 5:30. Isaacz; parents: Abraham Isaacsz Plancken; witnesses: Mr. Hans Kierstede, Secy. Corn. Van Tienhoven, Maurice Janszen, Rachel Vynen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Susanna Verplanck , daughter of Abraham Isaacsen Verplanck and Maria Vigne, on 25 May 1642 at Reformed Dutch Church, New Amsterdam, (sponsors Jan Janszen dam, Mr. Hans Kierstede, Christina Vynen).
2 CONT Ibid., 5:31. Susanna; parents: Abraham Isaacsz Planck; witnesses: Jan Janszen dam, Mr. Hans Kierstede, Christina Vynen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Pieter van Mansvelt , son of Hans van Mansvelt, on 10 August 1642 at Reformed Dutch Church, New Amsterdam, (sponsors Jeurge Roelofszen, Sergt; Pieter Pye, Mr. Hans Kierstede, Sara Roelofs, Maria Lievens, T
2 CONC ryntje Elberts).
2 CONT Ibid., 5:32. Pieter; parents: Hans Van Mansvelt; witnesses: Jeurge Roelofszen, Sergt., Pieter Pye, Mr. Hans Kierstede, Sara Roelofs, Maria lievens, Tryntie Elberts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Daniel Adamszen , son of Adam Roelantsen, on 3 February 1644 at Reformed Dutch Church, New Amsterdam, (sponsors Mr. Michael Hoykens, Mr. Hans Kierstede, olof Stephenszen van Courtlt, Anneken Loockermans).
2 CONT Ibid., 5:34. Daniel; parents: Adam Roelantszen; witnesses: Mr. Michiel Hoykens, Mr. Hans Kierstede, olof Stephenszen Van Courtlt., Anneken Loockermans.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Catherine Van der Beek , daughter of Paulus Van der Beek and Maria Badie, on 10 September 1645 at Reformed Dutch Church, New Amsterdam, (sponsors: De Hr. Willem Kieft, gouvernor, Mr. Hans Kierstede, Willem
2 CONC  Brendenbent, and Aeltje Braconje, and Maritie Lievens).
2 CONT Ibid., 5:86 Catharyn; parents: Mr. Paulus, Chirurgin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Marretje Jacobse Cool , daughter of Jacob Barentsen Cool and Marretje Symens, on 7 March 1666 at Old Dutch Church, Kingston, Ulster Co., New York, (sponsors Hans Cheyrstede, Annetje Tyssen, Anna Blom).
2 CONT Roswell Randall Hoes, editor, Baptismal and Marriage Registers of the Old Dutch Church of Kingston, Ulster County, New York, 1660-1809 (Baltimore, MD: Genealogical Publishing Co., 1891, 1980, 1997), page 5, no. 68. Arent, Marretje
2 CONC ; parents: Jacob Barentsen Cool, Marretje Symens.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Sara Abrahamse Moll , daughter of Abraham Lambertszen Moll and Jacomyntje Jacobs, on 15 October 1666 at Reformed Dutch Church, New York City, New York, (sponsors Hans Kieertede, Marritje Lamberts).
2 CONT "Records of the Reformed Dutch Church in New York", New York Genealogical and Biographical Record Vols.5- (1874-): 7:72. Sara; parents: Abraham Lambertszen, Jacomyntie Jacobs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Neeltje Gysbertse , daughter of Gysbert Albertszen and Willemtie Claes, on 13 April 1667 at Reformed Dutch Church, New York City, New York, (sponsors Mr. Hans Kierstede, Jannetie Kierstede).
2 CONT Ibid., 7:75. Neeltje; parents: Gysbert Elbertszen, Willemtje Claes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Johannes Jacobsz Van der Grift , son of Jacob Leendertszen Van der Grift and Rebecca Fredricx, on 26 June 1667 at Reformed Dutch Church, New York City, New York, (sponsors Jan Evertszen Bout, Mr. Hans Kier
2 CONC stede, Tryntie Simons, Jannestie Kierstede).
2 CONT Ibid., 7:75. Johannes; parents: Jacob Leendertszen, Rebecca Fredricks.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by Sara Roelofse b. 5 Apr 1627, d. between 7 Aug 1693 and 21 Oct 1693:
2 CONT Hans Kierstede b. 21 Sep 1644, d. 14 May 1691
2 CONT Ibid., 5:85.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roeloff Kierstede b. 1 Jan 1647
2 CONT Ibid., 5:88.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Kierstede b. 23 Apr 1651, d. in infancy
2 CONT Ibid., 5:96.
2 CONT
2 CONT Blandina Kierstede b. 8 Jun 1653, d. 1702
2 CONT Ibid., 5:149. Parents Mr. Hans Van Kierstede, Sara Roelofs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jocham Kierstede b. 24 Oct 1655, d. 1710
2 CONT Ibid., 5:155. Parents Mr. Hans Van Kierstede, Sara Roelofs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucas Kierstede b. 23 Sep 1657, d. between 1693 and 16 Apr 1711
2 CONT Ibid., 5:181. Lucas; parents: Mr. Hans Kierstede, Sara Roelofs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cathryn Kierstede b. 4 Jan 1660/61
2 CONT Ibid., 6:46. Catharyn; parent: Mr. Hans Kierstede.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Kierstede b. 4 Jun 1662, d. before Nov 1663
2 CONT Ibid., 6:149. Jacob; parents: Mr. Hans Kierstede, Sara Roelofs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Kierstede b. 28 Nov 1663, d. before 9 Jan 1702
2 CONT Ibid., 6:155. Jacobus; parents: Mr. Hans Kierstede, Sara Roelofs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel Kierstede b. 13 Sep 1665
2 CONT Ibid., 7:26. Rachel; parents: Hans Kierstede, Sara Roelofs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Kierstede died before 1 September 1669 (wife remarried).
2 CONT Samuel S. Purple, Records of the Reformed Dutch Church in New Amsterdam and New York; Marriages from 11 December 1639 to 26 August 1801 (Bowie, MD: Heritage Books, reprint 2003, original 1890 NYG&BS), p.34. Cornelis Van Borsum, j.
2 CONC m. Van't Veer op Breuckelen, en Sara Roelofs, Wede., Van Hans Kierstede.
2 CONT
