2 NOTE Malcolm and others.. Another revealing graphic is: https://graphcommons.com/graphs/9caebf55-e107-4cf4-9c43-d8741cfd6d95?sel=08cf201a-bea5-436d-ae94-72777b4f0bcb which goes along with the https://www.geni.com/projects/Castello-Plan
3 CONC /39952 Project
2 NOTE Roeloff Janson (Jans) and Anneke Jans lived in the house at the base of Whitehall Street during their years of marriage.  Once Roeloff died and Anneke remarried Everardus Bogardus, the Dutch Reformed Church Minister, they moved in
3 CONC side the Fort, to the Rectory, next to the Church.  When Reverend Everardus Bogardus died at sea, Anneke left the Rectory.  She may have spent a short time back at her home on Whitehall Street.  However, she soon moved to Beverwyc
3 CONC k (Albany), to live out the rest of her life.  Her eldest daughter Sarah Roeloffson married Hans Kierstede, M.D. and they took over the property on Whitehall Street.  The Rectory inside the Fort was later to become the home of Stu
3 CONC yvesant and many other leaders of the City.  Governor Lovelace lived there when the English took control.
