1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Freiherr von Trachenberg, Herr auf Drum und Ronow.
2 CONT
2 CONT In July 1564, Ferdinand I, Holy Roman Emperor, died.  He was succeeded by his son Maximilian II, who sent diplomats Andreas Dudith and Wilhelm von Kurzbach to reconcile Sigismund II Augustus of Poland with his wife Catherine (Maxi
2 CONC milian’s sister).  If unsuccessful, the diplomats were to convince Sigismund to allow Catherine to leave Poland.  Sigismund eventually allowed Catherine to depart.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilhelm was a subject of Maximilian (who was King of Bohemia) and an important Bohemian noble.  His family’s history of supporting the Jagellonian dynasty in Poland, Hungary, and Bohemia probably made him a good choice as an envoy
2 CONC .
