2 CONT It's recorded that I was born "Sarah Jans Roelofs" on September 3, 1632 and when I was old enough to do so, I married Dr. Hans Keigtda.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-55650/scandinavian-immigrants-in-new-york-1630-1674?action=showRecord&itemId=145&groupId&indId=externalindividual-3d588f503c59acde1df531ea438684bd&callback_token=pKdltPhFafbMF9hNlz7
2 CONC hO3Zyf8FgvPT4l96RAzzq&mrid=3e0d85c8dee5229c6327e8734eff5c60 Sara Roeloffse - her 'Will'...] ; *This can only be seen/read by MyHeritage members
2 CONT * [http://resources.huygens.knaw.nl/vrouwenlexicon/lemmata/data/Roelofs huygens.knaw.nl...] ; [http://resources.huygens.knaw.nl/vrouwenlexicon/lemmata/data/jans huygens.knaw.nl...] ; 
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''ROELOFS, Sara''' (geb. Amsterdam ?-4-1627 – gest. New York ?-9-1693), trad in Nieuw-Nederland op als tolk in onderhandelingen met Indianen. Dochter van '''Roelof Jansz'''. (1601/02-1637), varensgezel en later pachtboer, en '''
2 CONC Anneke Jans''' (1604/05-1663), de '''mythische stammoeder''' van Nieuw-Nederland.  Sara Roelofs trouwde
2 CONT ># (1) op 29-6-1642 in Nieuw-Amsterdam met '''Hans Kierstede''' (ca. 1612-1666), scheepschirurgijn bij de WIC; 
2 CONT ># (2) op 1-9-1669 in Nieuw-Amsterdam met '''Cornelis van Borsum''' (gest. 1682), landeigenaar op Manhattan en uitbater van het veer naar Long Island; 
2 CONT >#(3) op 21-7-1683 in New York met '''Elbert Elbertsz Stouthoff''', koopman en officier van de schutterij. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Uit huwelijken geboren kinderen===
2 CONT *(1) werden 6 zoons en 4 dochters, uit (2) werd 1 dochter geboren.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Literatuur===
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Documents relative to the colonial history of the State of New York, 13, E.B. O’Callaghan ed. (Albany 1881).
2 CONT *  Howard S.F. Randolph, ‘The Kierstede family’, New York Genealogical and Biographical Record 65 (1934) 224-233, 329-338.
2 CONT *  P.J. Risseeuw, Anneke Jans. Een roman uit de jaren toen New York nog Nieuw Amsterdam was (Kampen 1958).
2 CONT *  John O. Evjen, Scandanavian immigrants in New York, 1630-1674 (Baltimore 1972) 105-108.
2 CONT *  Lois M. Feister, ‘Linguistic communication between the Dutch and Indians in New Netherland’, Ethnohistory 20 (1973) 1, 25-38.
2 CONT *  David M. Riker, ‘Surgeon Hans Kierstede of New Amsterdam’, De Halve Maen 57 (1983) 3, 11-13, 24.
2 CONT *  Willem Frijhoff, Wegen van Evert Willemsz. Een Hollands weeskind op zoek naar zichzelf, 1607-1647 (Nijmegen 1995), passim.
2 CONT *  Mark P. Meuwese, ‘For the peace and well-being of the country’: intercultural mediators and Dutch-Indian relations in New Netherland and Dutch Brazil, 1600-1664 (ongepubliceerde diss., Notre Dame Univ., Indiana, 2003) 408-410, 
2 CONC 444-447
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *Married in New Amsterdam ath the Dutch Reformed Church
2 CONT *''1642 29 Jun''; '''Hans Kierstede''', jm van Maegdenburg; '''Sara Roelofs''', jd van Amsterdam, beyde wonende tot N. Amsterdam
2 CONT *''1669 01 Sep''; '''Cornelis van Borsum''', jm van't Veer op Breuckelen; '''Sara Roelofs''', wid Hans Kierstede
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Sara was baptized on 5 April 1627 in Amsterdam, North Brabant, The Netherlands.
2 CONT * Sara's birth, baptism, and death information is available at https://worldconnect.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=4651&id=I11467
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Daughter of Roeloff Jansen and Anneke Jans. John Reynolds Totten, "Anneke Jans (1607-8?-1663) and Her Two Husbands", New York Genealogical & Biographical Record Vol. 56, pages 202-243 (1925): p.208. Born about 1625 or earlier, die
2 CONC d 1693.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sara Roelofse was baptized on 5 April 1627 at Lutheran Church, Amsterdam, Noord Holland, Netherlands, sponsors Assueris Jansen, Stijntje Barents. William Brower Bogardus, Dear "Cousin": A Charted Genealogy of the Descendants of An
2 CONC neke Jans Bogardus (1605-1663) to the 5th Generation - and of her sister, Marritje Jans (Wilmington, OH, U.S.A.: Anneke Jans and Everardus Bogardus Descendants Association, 1996), chart no.1. George Olin Zabriskie, "Anneke Jans in
2 CONC  Fact and Fiction", New York Genealogical and Biographical Record Vol. 104, pp. 65-72, 157-164 (1973): 104:67.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 1st at Reformed Dutch Church, New Amsterdam, on 29 June 1642 Hans Kierstede "Mr. Hans Kierstede, Chirurgyn, j.m. Van Maegdenburg, en Sara Roelofs, j.d. Van Amsterdam, beyde wonende tot N. Amsterdam." Samuel S. Purple, 
2 CONC Records of the Reformed Dutch Church in New Amsterdam and New York; Marriages from 11 December 1639 to 26 August 1801 (Bowie, MD: Heritage Books, reprint 2003, original 1890 NYG&BS), p.11.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Isaac du Trieux , son of Philippe du Trieux and Susanna du Chesne, on 24 April 1642 at Reformed Dutch Church, New Amsterdam, (sponsors Mr. Herman Reyniers, Jan Willemszen Schut, Philip Gerritsz., Sara du T
2 CONC rieux, Sara Roelofs). "Records of the Reformed Dutch Church in New York", New York Genealogical and Biographical Record Vols.5- (1874-): 5:31. Jsaacsen; parents: Philip du' Trieux; witnesses: Mr. Herman Reyniers, Jan Willemszen Sc
2 CONC hut, Philip Gerritsz, Sara du Trieux, Sara Roelofs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Pieter van Mansvelt , son of Hans van Mansvelt, on 10 August 1642 at Reformed Dutch Church, New Amsterdam, (sponsors Jeurge Roelofszen, Sergt; Pieter Pye, Mr. Hans Kierstede, Sara Roelofs, Maria Lievens, T
2 CONC ryntje Elberts). Ibid., 5:32. Pieter; parents: Hans Van Mansvelt; witnesses: Jeurge Roelofszen, Sergt., Pieter Pye, Mr. Hans Kierstede, Sara Roelofs, Maria lievens, Tryntie Elberts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Jessen de Foreest , son of Isaac de Foreest and Sarah du Trieux, on 9 November 1642 at Reformed Dutch Church, New Amsterdam, (witnesses: Jochem Pieterszen, Philip du trieux, Madam de La montagne, Sara Roel
2 CONC ofs). Ibid., 5:32. Jessen; parents: Isacq de Foreest; witnesses: Jochem Pieterszen, Philip du trieux, Madam de La montagne, Sara Roelofs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnessed the baptism of Melchior Uldericks Kleyn , son of Uldrick Kleyn and Baefje Pieters, on 23 November 1642 at Reformed Dutch Church, New Amsterdam, (sponsors Jacob Swart, Sara Roelofs). Ibid., 5:32. Mechior; parents: Ulderic
2 CONC k Cleen; witnesses: Jacob Swart, Sara Roelofs.
